      "content": "Blue light definitely has a shorter wavelength than red light! 📉\n\nNow, look at the equation $\\sin\\theta = \\frac{\\lambda}{d}$. Notice that $\\lambda$ is in the numerator on the right side. When $\\lambda$ decreases, what happens mathematically to $\\sin\\theta$?"
